MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_001: Alexandra. Sorry to bother you, but does this\nhandwriting seem familiar at all?
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_002: Hm? Oh! I believe that's my uncle's!
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_003: Yes...he's writing me to propose you and I get\nmarried. I take it you weren't informed.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_004: Ugh, not this again. I'm sorry I didn't say anything.\nHe promised me that he was going to let this go!
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_005: No, no apology needed. I just wanted to make sure.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_006: This letter was given to me by my servant—I was\nsure there had to be some mistake.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_007: A young woman of fine breeding, and a man reeking\nof blood? It's plain we'd be an ill fit.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_008: Well, it wasn't delivered by mistake. It was my\nuncle's desire that we marry.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_009: Believe it or not, at the Heroic Games he was pulling\nall kinds of strings, trying to make it into a reality.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_010: Interesting. I'd heard he was known for his\ngamesmanship—just never thought I'd be the object.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_011: My uncle had a certain amount of clout within the\ntemple, but his ambitions were not easily satisfied.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_012: He hoped to gain influence over state as well, so he\nset his gaze on Brezarant, in all its turmoil.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_013: Ahh. That explains it. I do carry the blood of Breza\nin my veins, dilute as it may be.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_014: Not to mention the intimate proximity to Duke\nChiron would have expanded his influence further.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_015: And my uncle is a busy man. If I were married and\nstarting a family, well, that's one less thing for him...
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_016: I see. He sought a convenient way to sink his claws\nin another house.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_017: Exactly. His hope was that I would win the Heroic\nGames and raise my profile.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_018: Right. Especially as my country places so much\nstore on martial valor.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_019: Just another one of his evil schemes. This is why I\nfinally decided to leave my uncle's house.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_020: I'm sorry you ever had to get involved in all this.\nFeel free to ignore this strange proposal.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_021: No, no. I know well how irksome it is when people\nmeddle in one's life like this.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_022: Well, I'll write him back posthaste notifying him of\nmy refusal.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_023: And I shall be sure to stress that he ought not to\nmake such propositions against his niece's wishes.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_024: Oh, no. There's no need to go to all that trouble for\nme, Gaitz.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_025: Happy to do it. I don't presume it will turn him\naround, but perhaps he'll be a mote less brazen.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_C_026: Then consider me in your debt. And thank you for\nlooking out for me.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_001: Hyah!
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_002: Oomph! You are skilled!
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_003: Your swordsmanship's something to behold. Clearly\nJurah's knights aren't an empty show of strength.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_004: I'm honored you noticed. We're constantly working\nto refine our fighting abilities.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_005: Still... Are you aiming to make yourself more suitable\nfor a marriage partner?
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_006: Not at all. My martial skills are for the sake\nof the divine Jurah.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_007: Of course, apologies. I just ask because you don't\nseem to be motivated by faith alone.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_008: They say Jurah would sit in her rocking chair all day\nlong, without speaking to another soul.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_009: A mere soldier like me could never fathom the\ncontents of a goddess's heart.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_010: But I believe we're supposed to do all we can to\nkeep the peace. That's what she would want.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_011: The time of Lord Solel's rule was peaceful, but we\nstill faced our fair share of bandits.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_012: I'm sure it brought Jurah comfort to have such\na skilled knight in her service.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_013: I can only hope that is true. My point was that even\nin times of peace, I continued to hone my skills.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_014: My uncle hoped to exploit my abilities, and I entered\nthe Heroic Games at his encouragement.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_015: Is that so? It's striking, how we walked these twisting\npaths toward each other's friendship.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_016: The purity of your devotion, your startling abilities...\nPerhaps I was too hasty.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_017: What do you mean, "too hasty"?
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_018: In refusing your uncle's marriage proposal. Perhaps I\nought to have paid it greater heed.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_019: Not that I'd care to serve his aims. But you are quite\nthe charming match.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_020: Oh no! Please don't tease me about all that again...
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_B_021: Ahahaha. Apologies! Pay me no mind.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_001: Excuse me, Gaitz! Do you recognize this handwriting\nand signature?
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_002: Hm? That looks to be my servant's script. Oh no.\nIs that letter saying... Ugh.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_003: Incredible, but not entirely unpredictable. This letter\nis a marriage proposal, between you and me.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_004: It seems my man forgot himself. He should never\nhave sent that.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_005: Ah, so it appears there is some secret plotting\nhappening in your household as well.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_006: Well... My parents are gone, and I am unwed.\nWhile I have no bloodmark, I am long-lived.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_007: I suppose he looked upon the circumstances of my\nlife and worried about my future.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_008: He would like me to have a family, that I might stave\noff loneliness.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_009: But I didn't realize he was sending proposals to\nany suitable partners.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_010: He probably thought I was a good target, especially\ngiven our previous history with proposals.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_011: Yes. Apologies—he's a good man, my servant, but he\ndoes tend to act rashly for my benefit.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_012: It's the same sort of ham-fistedness you might\nrecognize in your uncle.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_013: I suppose this is what you were talking about before\nwhen you said you know all about meddling.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_014: Yes, this is what I meant. At any rate, please,\ndisregard this letter.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_015: Not at all. I'm going to write a proper letter\nof refusal.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_016: I will be sure to communicate that Mr. Gaitz has\nno need to be concerned about his marital status.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_017: He is an excellent fighter and has many friends. \nThere's not much chance of him getting lonely.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_018: Oh. Well. I'm honored to hear you say that.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_019: And in truth, I'd be relieved for the intervention.\nI'm tiring of his attempts at matchmaking.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_020: I have to admit, the reversal of our roles is a bit\nhumorous.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_021: Heehee. Then you wouldn't mind if I took this\nopportunity to tease you a bit?
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_022: What do you mean by that?
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_023: Nothing. I'm just realizing that perhaps I was too\nhasty in refusing your offer of marriage.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_024: I don't like being a pawn in anyone's scheme, but\nthen again...you are quite the charming match.
MID_SE_Gat_Ale_A_025: Ahem! Quite a severe response for some teasing,\ndon't you think?